2 CONT
2 CONT Marquis Xian of Jin (Chinese: 晉獻侯; pinyin: Jìn Xiàn Hóu), personal name Ji Ji or Ji Su, was a marquis of the Jin state.[1][2] He was preceded by his father, Marquis Xi, and succeeded by his son, Marquis Mu.
