1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zheng_(state)
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Cheng of Zheng (鄭成公, 睔) was a ruler of the State of Zheng during ancient China. He was born around 610 BCE and passed away in 571 BCE. He was the son of Duke Xiang of Zheng (鄭襄公, 堅) and the father of Duke Li of Zheng (鄭釐公, 髡頑
2 CONC  惲). His siblings included Duke Dao of Zheng (鄭悼公, 沸) and Prince Xu of Zheng (君繻, 公子繻).
2 CONT
2 CONT The State of Zheng was a significant regional power during the Spring and Autumn period, often involved in conflicts with neighboring states. Duke Cheng's lineage was part of the House of Ji, which was connected to the Royal House
2 CONC  of Zhou.
