1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=28160 '''Zheng Bolin''' 鄭白麟] [28160] According to the Pujiang ZL (1526), 7.5a entry for Zheng(1) Qi [28161], Bolin was his 21st generation ancestor (i.e. F+19). A
2 CONC ccording to XTS, 75A.5a-5b, Bolin was the eldest son of Shimao [28159], when the lineage split into seven branches (fang 房) and that the senior branch, i.e. Bolin's branch), was cut off. According to Qi's biograhies the family mov
2 CONC ed from Rongyang to She Xian, from Shexian to Mu Zhou (Jiande Xian) and then to Pujiang. Since Bolin was active around the end of the Northern Wei, it would not be suprising if he were the first one who moved south and I so indica
2 CONC te since this was a period of immigration to She Xian. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
