2 PLAC Taiyuan, Shanxi, China
2 ADDR
1 OCCU founding Emperor of Tang Dynasty
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Emperor Gaozu of Tang (566-635) was the founder and first emperor of this great dynasty. He was born Li Yuan, and given the courtesy name of Shude. He took the name Gaozu, meaning High Founder or Progenitor, upon e
2 CONC stablishing the Tang Dynasty in 618.... Reference: http://totallyhistory.com/emperor-gaozu-of-tang/
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Gaozu_of_Tang
2 CONT
2 CONT Emperor Gaozu of Tang (8 April 566 – 25 June 635), born Li Yuan, courtesy name Shude, was the founder of the Tang Dynasty of China, and the first emperor of this dynasty from 618 to 626. Under the Sui dynasty, Li Yuan was the gove
2 CONC rnor in the area of modern-day Shanxi, and was based in Taiyuan.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 615, Li Yuan was assigned to garrison Longxi. He gained much experience by dealing with the Göktürks of the north and was able to pacify them. Li Yuan was also able to gather support from these successes and, with the disintegr
2 CONC ation of the Sui dynasty in July 617, Li Yuan – urged on by his second son Li Shimin (the eventual Emperor Taizong) – rose in rebellion. Using the title of "Great Chancellor" (大丞相), Li Yuan installed a puppet child emperor, Empero
2 CONC r Gong, but eventually removed him altogether and established the Tang Dynasty in 618 as Emperor. His son and successor Li Shimin honoured him as Gaozu ("high founder") after his death.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=13059 '''Li Yuan''' 李淵] [13059] See XTS, 70A.1a ff. 《唐代人物知識ベース》記其生卒年為：566 - 635. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
